  "Number": 2,
  "Question": "For all nonzero real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) such that \\(x-y=xy,\\) \\(\\frac1x-\\frac1y\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\frac1{xy}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\frac1{x-y}\\)",
    "C": "\\(0\\)",
    "D": "\\(-1\\)",
    "E": "\\(y-x\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Combining the reciprocals reveals the difference \\(x-y\\) from the given equation. Since \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) are nonzero, \\(xy\\ne0\\), and\n\\[\n\\frac1x-\\frac1y\n=\\frac{y-x}{xy}\n=-\\frac{x-y}{xy}\n=-\\frac{xy}{xy}\n=\\boxed{-1}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
